{"book":23,"chapter":53,"context":{"chapter":53,"title":"The Suffering Servant","summary":"The Servant grows up unnoticed, is despised and rejected, and carries the griefs and sins of others. Silent as a lamb led to slaughter, he is cut off and buried, yet God accepts his life as an offering for sin, and he sees his offspring and justifies many.","background":"Few Old Testament passages are quoted or echoed in the New Testament as often. Philip explains it as speaking of Jesus (Acts 8:32-35), and Peter applies it to the cross (1 Peter 2:22-25). Jewish interpreters have often read the servant as Israel suffering among the nations. The Great Isaiah Scroll from the Dead Sea Scrolls, copied before Jesus' birth, contains this chapter.","customs":[{"term":"An offering for sin","verses":"53:10","note":"The Hebrew is asham, the guilt offering, a sacrifice that made amends for wrongdoing (Leviticus 5:14-19)."}],"watchFor":["The contrast between 'we… our… us' and 'he… him' (vv. 4–6).","In Hebrew, v. 6 begins and ends with 'all of us.'","'He was numbered with the transgressors' (v. 12), quoted in Luke 22:37."],"connections":["Acts 8:32-35","1 Peter 2:22-25","Luke 22:37","Matthew 8:17"]},"verses":{"1":{"w":[["מִי","mi","H4310","HPi","who?"],["הֶאֱמִין","he'emin","H539","HVhp3ms","has he believed"],["לִשְׁמֻעָתֵנוּ","lishmu'atenu","H8052","HR/Ncfsc/Sp1bp","<to> report our"],["וּזְרוֹעַ","uzeroa'","H2220","HC/Ncfsc","and [the] arm of"],["יְהוָה","yahweh","H3068","HNpt","Yahweh"],["עַל","'al-","H5921","HR","to"],["מִי","mi","H4310","HPi","whom?"],["נִגְלָתָה","niglatah","H1540","HVNp3fs","has it been revealed"]],"x":[[43012038,43012038,76],[45010016,45010017,54],[46001018,46001018,28],[43001012,43001012,20],[40016017,40016017,19],[40011025,40011025,16],[46001024,46001024,15],[23052010,23052010,14],[23040005,23040005,13],[43001007,43001007,13]],"xn":14},"2":{"w":[["וַיַּעַל","vaiya'al","H5927","Hc/Vqw3ms","and he grew up"],["כַּיּוֹנֵק","kaiyonek","H3126","HRd/Ncmsa","like <the> sh